4,44,Position comparison output pulse width setting,"Set the pulse width of the signal that is output for position comparison.
The signal is not output when 0 is set.",113
4,45,Position comparison output polarity selection,"Set the polarity of position comparison output by bit setup for each output terminal.
[Setup bits]
  bit0:SO1, OCMP1
  bit1:SO2, OCMP2
  bit2:SO3, OCMP3",152
,,,"[Setup values of Each setting bit]
  0:The output photocoupler is turned ON for SO1 to 3 and is set to L level for OCMP1 to 3, respectively, during pulse output.",161
,,,"  1:The output photocoupler is turned OFF for SO1 to 3 and is set to H level for OCMP1 to 3, respectively, during pulse output.",127
,,," Basically, use this function as 0.",35
4,47,Pulse output selection,"Select the signal to be output from the pulse output terminal or Position comparison output terminal.
 0:Feedback scale output signal
 1:Position comparison output signal",170
