,,," bit0 Set up RTEX communication data size
  0:16-byte mode  1:32-byte mode
 bit1 Specifies synchronization mode among multiple axes using TMG_CNT.
  0:Semi synchronization among axes.
  1:Full synchronization among axes.",220
,,," bit2 For manufacturer's use, Fix at 0.
 bit3 Not used, Fix at 0.
 bit4 For manufacturer's use, Fix at 0.
 bit5 Command pulse saturation function selection
  0:Invalid  1:Valid",176
,,," bit6 Return to origin operation velocity restriction function activation
  0:Invalid  1:Valid
 bit7-10 Not used, Fix at 0.
 bit11-13 For manufacturer's use, Fix at 0.
 bit14-15 Not used, Fix at 0.",197
,,,"* Set up the RTEX communication cycle properly according to the specifications of the host device.
  If the parameter is not proper, the operation is not be guaranteed.",168
7,23,RTEX function extended setup 2,Sets each RTEX functions by bit unit.,37
,,," bit0 Parameter writing through RTEX communication
  0:Enable  1:Disable
 bit1 Alarm code sub number setup
  0:Fixed to 0.
  1:Sub number enabled.",146
,,," bit2 RTEX status response condition setting while sequence upon inputting of over-travel inhibition is disabled (Pr5.04 = 1).
  0:Status enabled  1:Fixed to 0
 bit3 RTEX status bit arrangement setup of POT/NOT
  0:POT is bit 1, NOT is bit 0.",242
,,,"  1:NOT is bit 1, POT is bit 0.
 bit4 Set up [COM] LED display mode
  0:Mode 1
  1:Mode 2
 bit5 Non-cyclic command start mode setting
  0:When standard command is changed.
  1:When command code and command parameter are changed.",228
,,," bit6 Set up POT/NOT RTEX status logic
  0:No inversion  1:Inversion
 bit7 PSL/NSL RTEX status logic setting
  0:Without reversing  1:With reversing
 bit8 RTEX status selection between In_Progress and AC_OFF
  0:In_Progress  1:AC_OFF",233
,,," bit9 Selects whether to return a command error in over-travel inhibit direction when a command is received after a deceleration stop caused by over-travel inhibit input.
  0:Command error is not returned.
  1:Command error is returned.",236
,,," bit10-13 Not used, Fix at 0.
 bit14 Command positional deviation [Command unit] output setting
  0:Internal command position(after filter) [Command unit] - Actual position[Command unit]",186
,,,"  1:Internal command position(before filter) [Command unit] - Actual position [Command unit]
 bit15 Not used, Fix at 0.",119
7,24,RTEX function extended setup 3,Sets each RTEX functions by bit unit.,37
,,," bit0 Specifies output status of EX-OUT1 during communication shut-down after RTEX communication is established.
  0:Held
  1:Initialized (Output when EX-OUT1 is 0.)",165
,,," bit1 Specifies output status of EX-OUT2 during communication shut-down after RTEX communication is established.
  0:Held
  1:Initialized (Output when EX-OUT2 is 0.)
 bit2 For manufacturer's use, Fix at 0.",205
,,," bit3 Setting condition for In_Position (positioning complete signal) of RTEX communication
  0:Unit is set up by Pr5.20.
  1:Command unit",138
,,," bit4 Setting condition for Servo_Active (servo-on state signal) of RTEX Communication *1
  0:Same as before
  1:Turns on in command receivable state after servo ON.",165
,,," bit5 The correction function for detection delay of latch position.
  0:The correction time of both the latch signal rising edge detection and the latch signal falling edge detection is set by Pr7.09",200
,,,"  1:The correction time of the latch signal rising edge detection is set by Pr7.09, the correction time of the latch signal falling edge detection is set by Pr7.92.
 bit6  Not used, Fix at 0.",191
,,," bit7 Select the state of the internal value of TFF from RTEX communication (Fall prevention in Servo-ON) *2
  0:Clear
  1:Hold the internal value
 bit8-10 For manufacturer's use, Fix at 0.
 bit11-15 Not used, Fix at 0.",219
,,,"*1 Pr7.40 (RTEX function extended setup 4) bit0 can be set up simultaneous, refer to it.",88
,,,"*2 The internal value is cleared at the timing of Servo-OFF, deceleration to stop due to over-travel inhibit input, stop and in safety state
   When this setting value is set to 1, set TFF to a value smaller than Pr5.11 (Thrust setup for emergency stop).",254
7,25,RTEX speed unit setup,"Set up the unit of speed data used in RTEX communication.
Set up the unit both for both command data such as command speed and for response data such as actual speed.",166
,,," 0:mm/s
 1:Command unit/s",25
7,26,RTEX continuous error warning setup,"Generates WngC0h (RTEX continuous error warning) when the No. of continuous errors reaches the setting of this parameter.
When the setting value is 0, this function is disabled and no warning is issued.",202
7,27,RTEX accumulated error warning setup,"Generates WngC1h (RTEX accumulated error warning) when the No. of accumulated errors reaches the setting of this parameter.
When the setting value is 0, this function is disabled and no warning is generated.",207
7,28,RTEX_Update_Counter error warning setup,"If Update_Counter is accumulated exceeding the setting value of this parameter and correct update fails, WngC2h (RTEX_Update_Counter error warning) is issued.
When the setting value is 0 or 1, this function is disabled and no warning is generated.",247
7,29,RTEX monitor select 1,"Select the monitor type of Response_Data1.
Please set up Type_Code (8 bits) of a RTEX monitor command.
If the setup value is 0, the actual position (APOS) is monitored.",168
7,30,RTEX monitor select 2,"Select the monitor type of Response_Data2 when non-cyclic command = 0h.
Please set up Type_Code (8 bits) of a RTEX monitor command.
If the setup value is 0, the actual speed (ASPD) is monitored.",194
7,31,RTEX monitor select 3,"Select the monitor type of Response_Data3 when non-cyclic command = 0h.
Please set up Type_Code (8 bits) of a RTEX monitor command.
If the setup value is 0, the thrust (TRQ) is monitored.",187
7,32,RTEX monitor select 4,"Select the monitor type of Sub_Response_Data1 when 32byte mode or sub-command = 0h.
Please set up Type_Code (8 bits) of a RTEX monitor command.
If the setup value is 0, 0 is returned.",183
7,33,RTEX monitor select 5,"Select the monitor type of Sub_Response_Data2 when 32byte mode.
Please set up Type_Code (8 bits) of a RTEX monitor command.
If the setup value is 0, 0 is returned.",163
7,34,RTEX monitor select 6,"Select the monitor type of Sub_Response_Data3 when 32byte mode.
Please set up Type_Code (8 bits) of a RTEX monitor command.
If the setup value is 0, 0 is returned",162
