Only 62500, 125000, 250000, 500000, 1000000 or 2000000 can be set. If other value is set, Err93.5 (Parameter setup error protection 4) occurs.",204
7,92,Correction time of latch delay 2,"Set the correction time for delay of the latch trigger signal detection.
This parameter can be switched by Pr7.24 bit5. ",120
,,," bit5 is 0:This parameter is disable.
 bit5 is 1:The correction time is reflected in the latch signal falling edge detection.",125
,,,"*Signal state of edge detection means the following
 The rising edge detection means the photocoupler is turned ON.
 The falling edge detection means the photocoupler is turned OFF.",181
7,93,Home position return limit speed,Set the limit speed for home position return operation.,55
,,,"If a value smaller than the internal minimum speed is set, the internal minimum speed is applied as limit speed.
If a value greater than the motor maximum speed is set, the motor maximum speed is applied as limit speed.",219
,,,"Note) The value is converted into command unit/s during internal computation.
The converted value is limited within the following range.
00000001h to 7FFFFFFFh (1 to 2147483647) 
If 0 is set for this parameter, 1 is internally set for control.",243
7,95,Number of RTEX continuous communication error protection 1 detections,"Set the number of RTEX continuous communication error protection 1 detections.
If a continuous CRC error occurs exceeding the number of times set for this parameter, Err83.0 (RTEX continues communication error protection 1) occurs.",231
,,,"If 0 or 1 is set for this parameter, 2 is internally set.",57
7,96,Number of RTEX continuous communication error protection 2 detections,Set the number of RTEX continuous communication error protection 2 detections.,78
,,,"If an interrupt omission, CRC error, MAC-ID error, C/R error or cyclic data error occurs exceeding the number of times set for this parameter, Err83.1 (RTEX continues communication error protection 2) occurs.",208
,,,"If 0 or 1 is set for this parameter, 2 is internally set.",57
7,97,Number of RTEX communication timeout error protection detections,Set the number of times for RTEX communication timeout error protection detection.,82
,,,"If 0 or 1 is set for this parameter, 2 is internally set.",57
7,98,Number of RTEX cyclic data error protection 1/2 detections,"Set the number of times for RTEX cyclic data error protection 1/2 detection.
If a continuous cyclic error occurs exceeding the number of times set for this parameter, Err86.0 or Err86.1 (RTEX cyclic data error protection 1 or 2) occurs.",236
,,,"If 0 or 1 is set for this parameter, 2 is internally set.",57
7,99,RTEX function extended setup 6,Sets each RTEX functions by bit unit.,37
,,," bit0 Activation of operation command (test run, FFT, etc.) execution by USB communication (PANATERM) when RTEX communication established
  0:Invalid  1:Valid
 bit1-2 For manufacturer's use, Fix at 0.",200
,,," bit3 Command pulse aggregate value [Command units] output setting
  0:Before filter  1:After filter
 bit4-6 For manufacturer's use, Fix at 0.
 bit7 RTEX monitor command regenerative load factor unit switching
  0:[%]  1:[0.1%]",227
,,," bit8-15 For manufacturer's use, Fix at 0.",42
7,100,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
7,108,RTEX communication synchronization setup,"Set the RTEX communication synchronization.
 0:Extended setup
 1-6:For manufacturer¡¯s use
 7:Normal setting",108
,,,"* Err96.4 is detected when a delay occurs in transmission/reception processing by the amplifier due to unstable transmission timing from the host device and so forth.
   If delay cannot be tolerated, please use this setting.",224
7,109,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
7,110,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
8,0,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
8,1,Profile linear acceleration constant,"Specifies acceleration during profile position control (PP).
Be sure to set before starting operation.",102
8,2,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
8,3,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
8,4,Profile linear deceleration constant,"Specifies deceleration during profile position control (PP).
Be sure to set before starting operation.",102
8,5,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
8,10,Amount of travel after profile position latch detection,Specifies the amount of travel during profile position latch positioning after a latch trigger signal input position is detected.,129
8,12,Profile return to home position mode setup,"Specifies a direction in which latch trigger signal is detected during profile home position return.
 0:Positive direction
 1:Negative direction
* For profile homing 2 or 4, select 0 setting. Setting to 1 also causes homing in positive direction.",246
8,13,Profile home position return velocity 1,"Specifies a velocity for high-speed operation during profile home position return.
Unit is specified with Pr7.25 (RTEX speed unit setup).
Maximum velocity is internally limited using Pr9.10 (Maximum over-speed level).",217
,,,"Note) When velocity setting is in mm/s, it is converted to command unit/s through internal computation and the equivalent value is limited within the range as shown below: 00000001h to 7FFFFFFFh (1 to 2147483647)",212
,,,"If setting value is 0, control is performed with an assumption that the setting value is 1.",91
8,14,Profile home position return velocity 2,"Specifies a velocity for low-speed operation during profile home position return.
Specify a minimum speed to decrease detection error.",134
,,,"Unit is specified with Pr7.25 (RTEX speed unit setup).
Maximum velocity is internally limited using Pr9.10 (Maximum over-speed level).",134
,,,"Note) When velocity setting is in mm/s, it is converted to command unit/s through internal computation and the equivalent value is limited within the range as shown below: 00000001h to 7FFFFFFFh (1 to 2147483647)",212
8,15,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
8,19,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
9,0,Motor type selection,Selects the motor type to be connected.,39
,,,"Note) The definition file currently selected in PANATERM is for linear.
If you are using the motor type with rotary, please select the model which is displayed ""DD"" at the end in model selection again.",201
9,1,Feedback scale resolution,Set up the resolution for the feedback scale.,45
9,2,Magnet pole pitch,Set up the magnet pole pitch.,29
9,3,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
9,4,Mass of motor's movable section,Set up the moving portion's mass of motor.,42
9,5,Rated motor thrust,Set up the rated thrust for the motor.,38
9,6,Rated effective motor current,Set up the rated effective current for the motor.,49
9,7,Maximum instantaneous motor current,Set up the maximum instantaneous current for the motor.,55
9,8,Motor phase inductance,Set up the phase inductance for the motor.,42
9,9,Motor phase resistance,Set up the phase resistance for the motor.,42
9,10,Maximum over-speed level,Set up the maximum over-speed for the motor.,44
9,11,Carrier frequency selection,"Select the carrier frequency.
 0:6kHz  1:12kHz  2:8kHz",54
9,12,Automatic current response adjustment,Set up the criteria for current response for the automatic setup of Pr9.13 (Proportional current gain) and Pr9.14 (Integral current gain).,138
9,13,Proportional current gain,Set up the proportional current gain.,37
9,14,Integral current gain,Set up the integral current gain.,33
9,17,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
9,18,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
9,19,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
9,20,Magnet pole detection scheme selection,Select the detection scheme for magnet pole position.,53
9,21,CS phase setup,Set up the phase difference between the induced voltage of the motor and the CS signal.,87
9,22,Magnet pole position estimation thrust command time,Set up the command thrust time for magnet pole position estimation.,67
9,23,Magnet pole position estimation command thrust,Set up the command thrust for magnet pole position estimation.,62
9,24,Magnet pole position estimation zero travel pulse width setup,Set up the zero travel pulse width for magnet pole position estimation.,71
9,25,Number of pulses for magnet pole position estimation motor stop judgment,Set up the number of pulses for motor stop judgment for magnet pole position estimation.,88
9,26,Time for magnet pole position estimation motor stop judgment,Set up the motor stop judgment time for magnet pole position estimation.,72
9,27,Time for magnet pole position estimation motor stop limitation,Set up the motor stop limitation time for magnet pole position estimation.,74
9,28,Magnet pole position estimation thrust command filter,"Set up the time constant for filter respective to the command thrust for magnet pole position estimation.
When this setting is zero, the filter is invalid and the command becomes a step command.",194
9,29,Overload protection timing characteristic selection,Select the overload protection timing characteristic from eight types of characteristics.,89
9,30,Number of pulses per magnet pole,"Linear motor information can be set in pulses, which is valid for linear-type settings.
This parameter cannot be used at the same time with Pr9.02(Magnet pole pitch). 
Use either of these parameters for setting.",211
9,31,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
9,32,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
9,33,For manufacturer's use,100 Please fix.,15
9,34,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13
9,35,Thrust saturation error protection frequency,"If thrust saturated is continued during a preset frequency, Err16.1(Thrust saturation error protection) will be activated.",122
,,,"If the setup value is 0, this function is disabled and an alarm will not be activated.
This parameter is enabled when the value set for Pr6.57 is 0.",148
9,48,Voltage feed forward gain 1,"Set a Voltage feed forward gain 1.
The higher the setting, the higher the current response to the change in thrust command becomes.",131
,,,"However, since it may cause oscillation or any other faulty operation, select an appropriate value according to the operating conditions. 
There is no compatibility with the automatic setting by the use of Pr9.12.",213
9,49,Voltage feed forward gain 2,"Set a Voltage feed forward gain 2.
The higher the setting, the higher the current response to thrust command.",109
,,,"However, since it may cause oscillation or any other faulty operation, select an appropriate value according to the operating conditions. 
There is no compatibility with the automatic setting by the use of Pr9.12.",213
